        "title": {
          "en": "Class list"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The teacher wrote on the board: girl, Meena, city, Chennai.\n\"Which names are special?\" she asked."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "common noun",
          "proper noun",
          "singular",
          "plural"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A common noun names any person, place or thing, like girl, city or book. A proper noun names one particular person or place and begins with a capital letter, like Meena and Chennai.\nSingular means one and plural means more than one. We usually add s: book and books. After s, x, ch and sh we add es: box and boxes, bus and buses.\nSome nouns change completely. Child becomes children and man becomes men."
        }
      },
